        "title": "Nonlinear Control",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Distributed systems analog:** Limit cycles are the mathematical name for resource contention oscillations. A service pool that oscillates between \"all threads busy, requests queuing\" and \"threads freed, burst dispatches\" is a self-sustained limit cycle — the Van der Pol energy balance (negative damping at low load pulls in more work; positive damping at high load sheds work) maps directly to this queue oscillation pattern."
